# Code Quality Standards

## File Naming

All source files use **kebab-case** with a mandatory layer suffix:

| Suffix | Example |
|---|---|
| `.entity.ts` | `client-membership.entity.ts` |
| `.value-object.ts` | `gym-org-name.value-object.ts` |
| `.use-case.ts` | `claim-membership.use-case.ts` |
| `.repository.ts` | `membership.repository.ts` (interface) |
| `.queries.ts` | `membership.queries.ts` (query interface) |
| `.controller.ts` | `membership.controller.ts` |
| `.routes.ts` | `membership.routes.ts` |
| `.schemas.ts` | `membership.schemas.ts` (Zod) |
| `.dto.ts` | `membership.dto.ts` |
| `.mapper.ts` | `membership.mapper.ts` |
| `.policy.ts` | `claim-membership.policy.ts` |

## Symbol Naming

- **Classes, Interfaces, Types, Enums:** `PascalCase` — `ClientMembership`, `MembershipRepository`, `MembershipStatus`
- **Variables, functions, methods, parameters:** `camelCase` — `findActiveByClient`, `gymOrgId`
- **Constants (compile-time fixed):** `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` — `MAX_ADMINS_PER_ORG`
- **Enum members:** `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` — `MembershipStatus.ACTIVE`
- **Private class fields:** `camelCase` with no underscore prefix — `private readonly gymOrgId: GymOrgId`

## Branded Domain ID Types

Every domain ID is a branded string — prevents accidental `gymOrgId` / `userId` swaps at compile time:

```ts
// ✅ correct — define in the owning feature's domain/
type GymOrgId = string & { readonly __brand: 'GymOrgId' };
type UserId    = string & { readonly __brand: 'UserId' };

function toGymOrgId(raw: string): GymOrgId {
  return raw as GymOrgId;
}
```

Never use plain `string` for domain identifiers in function signatures or entity fields.

## Value Object Pattern

Value Objects must be impossible to instantiate in an invalid state:

```ts
// ✅ correct
class GymOrgName {
  private constructor(readonly value: string) {}

  static create(input: string): GymOrgName {
    const trimmed = input.trim();
    if (!trimmed) throw new Error('GymOrgName cannot be empty');
    if (trimmed.length > 255) throw new Error('GymOrgName max 255 chars');
    return new GymOrgName(trimmed);
  }
}

// ❌ wrong — public constructor, mutable field, no validation
class GymOrgName {
  constructor(public value: string) {}
}
```

Rules:
- `private constructor` always
- `static create()` as the only factory — throw `Error` on invalid input
- All fields `readonly`
- No mutator methods; produce a new instance for changes
- Zod schemas must delegate to `create()` via `superRefine`, never re-implement the rule

## Entity Pattern

Entities carry identity and enforce lifecycle invariants:

```ts
class ClientMembership {
  private constructor(
    readonly id: MembershipId,
    private status: MembershipStatus,
    // ...
  ) {}

  static reconstitute(data: MembershipData): ClientMembership { /* from persistence */ }
  static create(cmd: CreateMembershipCommand): ClientMembership { /* new instance */ }

  activate(): void {
    if (this.status === MembershipStatus.ACTIVE) throw new AlreadyActiveError();
    this.status = MembershipStatus.ACTIVE;
  }
}
```

Rules:
- Must enforce state transitions — never expose raw setters that bypass invariants
- Must not be a pure data container (if there are no invariants, use a DTO instead)
- Must not import Express, Supabase, Pino, or infrastructure packages

## Constructor Injection

```ts
// ✅ correct — explicit dependencies, mockable in tests
class ClaimMembershipUseCase {
  constructor(
    private readonly membershipRepo: MembershipRepository,
    private readonly clock: Clock,
    private readonly idGen: IdGenerator,
  ) {}
}

// ❌ wrong — hidden dependency, impossible to unit test
class ClaimMembershipUseCase {
  private readonly membershipRepo = new SupabaseMembershipRepository();
}
```

- All required collaborators in the constructor
- No `new ConcreteImplementation()` inside use cases, services, or other use cases
- `process.env` must not be read inside any class — pass `config: AppConfig` instead

## TypeScript Strictness

- **No `any`** — use `unknown` and narrow with type guards. If `any` is truly unavoidable, add `// eslint-disable-next-line @typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any` with a one-line comment explaining why.
- **No non-null assertion (`!`)** without a guard comment explaining the guarantee.
- **No implicit returns** from async functions — always `return` or `throw`.
- `tsconfig.json` must have `"strict": true` and `"noUncheckedIndexedAccess": true`.

## SOLID Quick-Reference

| Principle | Rule for this project |
|---|---|
| **S** Single Responsibility | One use case = one business command or query. One controller action = one use-case call. |
| **O** Open/Closed | New provider → new adapter implementing existing port. New plan type → new Value Object / strategy, not a growing `switch`. |
| **L** Liskov Substitution | A repository implementation must honor every guarantee the interface declares — no `throw new NotImplemented()` for methods the interface promises. |
| **I** Interface Segregation | Command repos and query interfaces are always separate. Never widen an interface to satisfy one new caller; add a second narrower interface instead. |
| **D** Dependency Inversion | Use cases depend on `MembershipRepository` (interface), never on `SupabaseMembershipRepository` (class). Wire the concrete in `composition.ts`. |
